BeyondFreq-L2I generator release

Project: Unbiased Object Detection Beyond Frequency with Visually Prompted Image Synthesis (ICLR2026)
Authors: Xinhao Cai, Liulei Li, Gensheng Pei, Tao Chen, Jinshan Pan, Yazhou Yao, Wenguan Wang.

Third-party provenance is retained separately from the BeyondFreq model and package names:

* The imported L2I source snapshot inherits code distributed by
  https://github.com/UTokyo-FieldPhenomics-Lab/DODA
  Copyright(c)2024 illrayy. MIT license: licenses/upstream-l2i-MIT.txt.
* The control architecture and sampler are adapted from ControlNet:
  https://github.com/lllyasviel/ControlNet
  Apache2.0 license: licenses/ControlNet-Apache-2.0.txt.
* The ldm architecture derives from Stable Diffusion and preserves source
  attribution comments. Original code/model terms:
  https://github.com/CompVis/stable-diffusion
  licenses/Stable-Diffusion-OpenRAIL-M.txt.
* The CLIP tokenizer vocabulary follows openai/clip-vit-large-patch14;
  tokenizer/text assets and code: licenses/CLIP-MIT.txt.

Modified files identify compatibility changes in their headers. The checkpoint
export changes serialization and public names only; it preserves all original
tensor names, values and dtypes. Model weights retain OpenRAIL-M restrictions.
